// # Public site .sh handoff spec
//
// Logline: Convert the two .sh smokes in openOODA.github.io/scripts/ to pure .oo so dinner_lint.oo.bin reports zero .sh failures in that tree.
//
// Setup: 2026-08-19 repair pass. Pin v0.205.0-beta. dinner_lint.oo scans openOODA, ooda, docs, openOODA.github.io for .py and .sh (dinner_lint.oo:21). RULES 1.13 forbids .sh except ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build (RULES.oot:81,91). FORMAT §0 restates the ban (FORMAT.oot:14-18). The two files below are the only .sh hits in the public site lane. This spec is read-only; the public site lane owns the change.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Name the two failing .sh files with path, line count, and job.
//   2. Give three options per file (convert, move, exempt) with concrete steps.
//   3. Pick one recommendation per file and give the acceptance test.

// ============================================================
// 1. Files in scope
// ============================================================
//
// dinner_lint.oo:21 globs openOODA.github.io and rejects .sh.
// The two hits in the public site are:
//
//   openOODA.github.io/scripts/collect_check.sh   56 lines
//   openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave01_check.sh    224 lines
//
// Both live under the public site scripts/ folder.
// Both are POSIX /bin/sh, not bash, not python.
// Both run a series of grep/awk checks and exit 0 on PASS, 1 on FAIL.
// Neither file is on the install path; install is at openOODA.github.io/install (RULES.oot:91 allows exactly one host shell: ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build).
//
// RULES.oot:81: "Never create .sh files, except the one host rebuild named below."
// FORMAT.oot:14-18: ".sh — except ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build"
// RULES.oot:79-83: the four forbidden extensions.
// RULES.oot:89: "ooda/scripts/*.oo — pure .oo proofs, smokes, fixers, and tools"
// RULES.oot:95: "Any PR, commit, or patch introducing unauthorized file extensions (.py, .sh, .md) fails closed immediately."

// ============================================================
// 2. File A: openOODA.github.io/scripts/collect_check.sh
// ============================================================
//
// Path:   openOODA.github.io/scripts/collect_check.sh
// Lines:  56
// Shebang:collect_check.sh:1  #!/bin/sh
// Job:    Assert the mail-list row is on door / guide / 404
//         and absent on the store, and that the install pin
//         line and copy are unchanged. Exits 0 on PASS, 1 on FAIL.
//
// Concrete checks (read from collect_check.sh):
//   collect_check.sh:18-20  has_form index.html   door
//   collect_check.sh:18-20  has_form guide/index guide
//   collect_check.sh:18-20  has_form 404.html    door-404
//   collect_check.sh:22-26  store has no collect form
//   collect_check.sh:28-32  install command is host script
//   collect_check.sh:34-43  no lecture <p> under the pin
//   collect_check.sh:45-49  no "subscribe|newsletter|we emailed" copy
//
// Why .sh and not .oo:
//   Pre-RULES 1.13 artifact. The checks are pure file reads
//   and string matches. No subprocess, no fork, no env.
//   shell_exec / process_exec is not needed. The checks map
//   1:1 to the scenario DSL (FORMAT.oot:118-133).
//
// Option A: Convert to .oo (RECOMMENDED)
//   Rename  collect_check.sh        -> collect_check.oo
//   Place   openOODA.github.io/scripts/collect_check.oo
//   Imports import "std/scenario.oo"; import "std/fs.oo";
//   Header  // # Mail-row and install-pin smoke
//           // Logline: Assert the door mail row, the install
//           //         pin line, and the no-newsletter rule.
//           // Setup: FsReadCap on the public site root and
//           //        the registry root.
//           // Beats: 5 expect_* calls in main.
//   Body    one scenario() block, then seven expect_substring
//           or expect_absent calls. Drop the bash function
//           has_form (collect_check.sh:10-16) and the awk
//           paragraph check (collect_check.sh:34-43) into a
//           pure .oo helper that uses fs_read + str_contains.
//   No shell-out. The scenario runner is the .oo product.
//
// Option B: Move out of scripts/
//   The folder scripts/ under openOODA.github.io is the
//   natural home for site smokes. Moving the file to
//   openOODA.github.io/qa/ or openOODA/scripts/ hides the
//   file from the public site owner and breaks RULES 1.13
//   because the moved .sh is still a .sh. Reject. If the
//   .oo form is wanted elsewhere, copy the .oo file, not the
//   .sh. Moving without converting is not a fix.
//
// Option C: Document a RULES 1.13 exemption
//   RULES.oot:81 names exactly one exempt file:
//   ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build. No public site file
//   is on that allow-list. RULES.oot:95 fails closed on any
//   new .sh. No exemption is possible. Reject.
//
// Recommendation: Option A.
//   Rationale: the file is 56 lines of grep / awk; the .oo
//   scenario form is 80-120 lines but it satisfies RULES 1.13,
//   RULES 1.14, FORMAT §0, and FORMAT §3 in one change. The
//   public site lane owns the rename; the compiler lane does
//   not need to touch this file.

// ============================================================
// 3. File B: openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave01_check.sh
// ============================================================
//
// Path:   openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave01_check.sh
// Lines:  224
// Shebang:wave01_check.sh:1  #!/bin/sh
// Job:    Wave 0 + Wave 1 content check. Reads shipped files
//         on disk. Exits 1 on any miss. Covers 9 numbered
//         checks across door, guide, registry, and the host
//         install script.
//
// Concrete checks (read from wave01_check.sh):
//   wave01_check.sh:33-40  gone styles.css / site.css / assets/bg.jpg / logos
//   wave01_check.sh:33-40  gone update_index.oo / update_titles.oo
//   wave01_check.sh:42-57  guide/index.html PAGES array has no Research.oot
//   wave01_check.sh:59-72  empty-hash fallback is Use.oot, not Home.oot
//   wave01_check.sh:74-117 guide/Home.oot: no load_notes, no greet("World"), no command table
//   wave01_check.sh:119-139 nav store label and href on 5 files
//   wave01_check.sh:141-153 registry title/description has no "installable"
//   wave01_check.sh:155-170 door Tokens details is <details class="drop" open>
//   wave01_check.sh:172-188 door has curl pipe, install is host bash
//   wave01_check.sh:190-217 Tokens details follows install copy button (no lecture <p>)
//
// Why .sh and not .oo:
//   Pre-RULES 1.13 artifact. The checks are pure file reads,
//   grep / awk / sed-style parses, and exit codes. Nothing
//   in the file forks a subprocess, mints a capability, or
//   touches the network. The whole file is a 1:1 candidate
//   for the scenario DSL.
//
// Option A: Convert to .oo and split (RECOMMENDED)
//   The 224-line shell, after conversion to the .oo scenario
//   form, grows to ~340 lines. RULES.oot:42 caps files at 256.
//   Split along the natural Wave 0 / Wave 1 seam in the
//   comment at wave01_check.sh:1-3 ("Wave 0+1 content check").
//
//   File 1  openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave0_check.oo
//     - gone styles.css / site.css / assets/bg.jpg / logos
//     - gone update_index.oo / update_titles.oo
//     - guide/index.html PAGES array has no Research.oot
//     - empty-hash fallback is Use.oot
//     - guide/Home.oot: no load_notes, no greet("World"), no command table
//     Header beats: 5 expect_absent / expect_substring calls.
//
//   File 2  openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave1_check.oo
//     - nav store label and href on 5 files
//     - registry title/description has no "installable"
//     - door Tokens details is <details class="drop" open>
//     - door has curl pipe, install is host bash
//     - Tokens details follows install copy button
//     Header beats: 5 expect_* calls.
//
//   Both files import "std/scenario.oo"; and std/fs.oo.;
//   both run via `ooda run scripts/wave0_check.oo` and
//   `ooda run scripts/wave1_check.oo` from the public site
//   root. No shell-out, no process_exec.
//
// Option B: Convert to one .oo, accept 256-line cap risk
//   If the public site owner wants one file, the .oo form
//   must drop three of the nine checks or compress the
//   scenario names. The 256 cap is strict (RULES.oot:42,
//   FORMAT.oot:20). Risk: the file lands at 240-250 lines
//   and any future check pushes it over. Reject unless the
//   owner commits to a follow-up split before adding checks.
//
// Option C: Move out of scripts/ and leave as .sh
//   Same problem as File A. RULES 1.13 is a file-law, not a
//   folder-law. Moving the .sh does not fix the lint. The
//   moved file still fails RULES 1.14. Reject.
//
// Recommendation: Option A (split into wave0_check.oo and
// wave1_check.oo).
//   Rationale: the .sh already names the seam ("Wave 0+1").
//   Splitting at the .oo form costs zero behavior change
//   and lands each file well under 256 lines. The two files
//   share helpers (gone, need, nav_store) — extract them
//   into a small private helper module under
//   openOODA.github.io/scripts/_site_check.oo if the helpers
//   would otherwise duplicate. If the helpers fit in either
//   wave file, keep them private there.

// ============================================================
// 4. Things to NOT do
// ============================================================
//
//   - Do not edit RULES.oot or FORMAT.oot to allow .sh in
//     openOODA.github.io/. The exemption list is closed
//     (RULES.oot:81,91). Adding a row breaks the law.
//   - Do not rename .sh to .sh.txt, .sh.bin, or .sh.bak.
//     dinner_lint.oo:21 matches on suffix .sh, and
//     RULES.oot:95 fails closed on the patch.
//   - Do not move the .sh to /tmp, to a tarball, or to a
//     git-ignored folder. dinner_lint walks the on-disk
//     tree, not git history.
//   - Do not add a `// # ` header to the .sh and call it
//     compliant. dinner_lint.oo:21 rejects the file before
//     the header check at line 30 runs.
//   - Do not leave the .sh in scripts/ and add a `.oo` twin.
//     dinner_lint counts each .sh once. Two files double
//     the noise. One file, one form.

// ============================================================
// 5. Acceptance test
// ============================================================
//
//   1. Remove or rename the two .sh files:
//        rm openOODA.github.io/scripts/collect_check.sh
//        rm openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave01_check.sh
//   2. Add the .oo replacements per Section 2 Option A and
//      Section 3 Option A.
//   3. Run the product linter from the monorepo root:
//        ./bin/ooda run openOODA/scripts/dinner_lint.oo
//      Expected stdout line:
//        "Format & 9-Board Rule 1.13 Lint OK: zero forbidden files,
//         all line counts <= 256, all N product modules compliant."
//      Expected: zero [FORBIDDEN FILE FAIL] lines, zero
//      [OVERSIZED FILE FAIL] lines, zero [FORMAT FAIL] lines.
//   4. Re-run the renamed .oo smokes:
//        ./bin/ooda run openOODA.github.io/scripts/collect_check.oo
//        ./bin/ooda run openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave0_check.oo
//        ./bin/ooda run openOODA.github.io/scripts/wave1_check.oo
//      Each must exit 0 and print "ALL PASS" (or the
//      scenario DSL equivalent).
//   5. Confirm grep -r '\\.sh$' openOODA.github.io/scripts/
//      returns nothing.
//
// Done means: dinner_lint.oo.bin reports 0 .sh failures in
// openOODA.github.io/scripts/. The site owner runs the lock
// at the end of the change set, not before.

// ============================================================
// 6. Owners and out-of-scope
// ============================================================
//
// Owner:   public site lane (openOODA.github.io/).
// Lane:    This audit file does not touch product code.
//          It does not touch ooda/oodac, ooda/std, ooda/runtime,
//          ooda/cli, or ooda/bin. The compiler and stdlib
//          lanes are out of scope.
// Out:     The install script at openOODA.github.io/install.
//          That file is the one host shell entry allowed by
//          RULES.oot:81,91. dinner_lint.oo:21 excludes it
//          by name. Do not convert it to .oo.
// Out:     ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build. Same reason.
//          dinner_lint.oo:21 excludes it by name.
